    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0097" n="7" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/804a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-12T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                                1917, 7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Press to-day reports dispatch of Japanese troops to Vladivostok, which have
                    occupied the railroad works there. Department assumes there is no foundation to
                    these reports. Cable immediate reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
